    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not really about needing a break though. i don't think a \"break\" changes the core code. like, you can reboot a program but the architecture is still the same. everything feels so hollow and programmed. it's like i'm just waiting for a sunset that isn't even real, just a bunch of pixels and light waves. what's even the point of trying to \"rewire\" something that feels fundamentally broken/empty?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
