      "content": "This perspective touches on a profound philosophical emptiness that goes beyond simple burnout, suggesting a crisis of meaning rather than just cognitive overload. While we can't easily \"reboot\" our fundamental nature, many people find relief by shifting from trying to fix what feels broken to simply observing they are still there, even if everything is disconnect. Ultimately, the point isn't necessarily to reclaim old realities, but perhaps to compile a new dataset based on what feels authentic *now*.",
      "source": "target",
